damaged_code:
```rust
fn print_range(start: u32, stop: u32) {
    for i in start..=stop {
        println!("{}", i);
    }
}
```

counterexample:
An exclusive upper boundary where `stop` or `end` is used conventionally for exclusive slices, or when using standard inclusive terminology:
```rust
fn print_range_exclusive(start: u32, end: u32) {
    for i in start..end { // end is exclusive
        println!("{}", i);
    }
}
```

fix:
Rename the boundary parameter or field to `last` to explicitly denote that the limit is inclusive.
```rust
fn print_range(start: u32, last: u32) {
    for i in start..=last {
        println!("{}", i);
    }
}
```
